cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or build upon the Constrained Delta Evolution (CDE) research
  framework, please cite this repository and the relevant versioned manuscript.
  A DOI and formal release date will be added after publication is confirmed.
type: software
title: >-
  Constrained Delta Evolution (CDE): A General Framework for Structural
  Search, Optimization, Metric Evolution, and Distributed Intelligence
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
  - name: GPT-Obot
abstract: >-
  Constrained Delta Evolution (CDE) is a proposed specifications-first
  research framework for exploring state spaces through generated deltas
  governed by explicit constraints, evaluation policies, and path semantics.
  It investigates adaptive M-to-N branching, multi-scale directional
  exploration, integration with search, dynamic programming and
  branch-and-bound, solution-metric co-evolution, distributed exploration,
  typed structural relay, and controlled recursive generator evolution.
  The research corpus comprises conceptual foundations, contracts,
  illustrative cases, open questions, testable hypotheses, and a validation
  roadmap. Claims of superior performance, generalization, or recursive
  self-improvement remain unverified until supported by reproducible evidence.
keywords:
  - constrained delta evolution
  - structural intelligence
  - state delta constraint
  - adaptive branching
  - structural search
  - combinatorial optimization
  - dynamic programming
  - branch and bound
  - metric co-evolution
  - distributed exploration
  - structural relay
  - collective learning
  - recursive self-improvement
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
